regfile eHISI_VDP_CV100 {
    name = "VDP (video display processor, Hi3516C V100 / Hi3518 V100)";
    desc = "Video display processor (VDP, called VOU in the interrupt table: interrupt 23) of the Hi3516C V100 and Hi3518A/C V100 at 0x205C0000 (64 KB, data sheet chapter 10.2). The Hi3518 V100 data sheet lists the same 113 registers (offset, name, bit fields identical). Standard-definition display subset: VSD1 video layer, G3 graphics layer, DSD (standard-definition channel), DATE TV encoder and DAC registers. [check] VSD1VFPOS and VSD1VLPOS are printed at 0x3068/0x306C in their description blocks but at 0x4068/0x406C in the register summary table; this regfile uses 0x4068/0x406C (the VSD1 layer base is 0x4000, the summary lists them directly after VSD1DFPOS 0x4060; the description offsets look copied from the VSD0 layer). Generated 2026-11-15 by scripts/rdl-extract/gen_m_cells.py from the data sheet register tables (ds_extract2 + description extraction from the PDF); PROVENANCE: PROVEN = offsets, names, bit fields, access and reset values from the data sheet tables; nothing here is hardware verified.

    Register sources: 113 registers from the data sheet (hi3516cv100--Hi3516C-Datasheet.txt, section 10.2.5). ";

